KG42.register("source_edge_archive-aa7a3525d77ad60df4e24a15",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001","paper":"05-double_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","rule_ref":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R005","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-d3b88931c4051195","target":"COMP-60fa17e84f308f18","source_occurrence_id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","target_occurrence_id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"05-double_auction::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","target_unit_id":"05-double_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Discriminatory k-DA in the studied P2P solar market, using historical prices for preference-factor or game-theoretic bidding. | Initialization of the seed signal for preference-factor and game-theoretic bidding in the studied P2P solar market. | The modeled game-theoretic bidding strategies for buyers and sellers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"b10097cdaf04fb5d0968faff741c9d5b3a052ea76bc39aec74061bc1cfe86ec8","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Contract performance, exchange or delivery conditions in this mechanism: Sealed bid/ask natural ordering; each winning pair trades at k times its buyer bid plus (1-k) times its seller ask; no common interval price.","target_definition":"Price updates/signals and participant decision feedback in this mechanism: Sealed bid/ask natural ordering; each winning pair trades at k times its buyer bid plus (1-k) times its seller ask; no common interval price.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Transactions during an auction interval supply the weighted-average historical price used as the reference signal for subsequent participant bidding decisions. Scope: Discriminatory k-DA in the studied P2P solar market, using historical prices for preference-factor or game-theoretic bidding. Condition: Subsequent auction intervals using the previous-hour market price.","expression":"P_{\\text{seed}} = \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{N_T} T_m^Q \\, T_m^P}{\\sum_{m=1}^{N_T} T_m^Q}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x_pseed"],"parameter_refs":["theta_TmQ","theta_TmP","theta_NT"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g01-ev-20","v141-b-g01-ev-12"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-13","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"3","anchor_text":"u ke In this study, a double auction is of interest so that both buyers and us sellers may submit bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this study, a double auction is of interest so that both buyers and sellers may submit bids to trade excess solar electricity. Offers from both buyers and sellers consist of bid/ask prices as well as quantity in kWh. These bid/ask prices are determined based on the proposed game-theoretic approaches, where the game is non-cooperative, non-zero-sum, and simultaneous-move. All agents strategically attempt to maximize self-interests; all agents submit sealed bids without knowledge of the actions of other players. For simplicity, a two-player game is considered where an individual buyer bids against all other buyers while an individual seller bids against all other sellers. Each participant has three strategies: to bid lower, same, or higher than the previous-hour market price. The degree of bidding deviation from the previous-hour market rate is determined by each agent's low and high preferences. These two preference factors for participant $i$ (i.e., $\\delta_i^{strategy}$) are generated via sampling a normal distribution with a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 0.15."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3","anchor_text":"prosumer bids at a random bid/ask price without any strategic antici- pation and disregards the hist","equation_id":"Eq. (10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Preference Factor: This resembles a household's preference to always submit offers more/less than the previous-hour market rate. Thus, bid/ask prices are generated from a discount/markup factor of the previous-hour market price. This behavior is modeled via sampling a normal distribution with a mean of 0.2 and standard deviation of 0.15 to assume that most buyers seek a 20% discount from market rates and most sellers seek a 20% premium from market rates."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3","anchor_text":"the interval: NT m = 1 TmQ *TmP Pseed = NT Q m = 1 Tm (10) Because Pseed is not available for the fi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Since discriminatory auction mechanisms do not have a uniform market clearing price at each auction interval, the historical market price is determined by the weighted average of all transactions during the interval:\nP_seed = (Σ_{m=1}^{N_T} T_m^Q * T_m^P) / (Σ_{m=1}^{N_T} T_m^Q)   (10)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-12","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.2","anchor_text":"j re BiQfill Cleared kWh quantity for buyer i ; ≤BiQ Qfill Qm Sj Cleared kWh quantity for seller j ;","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 3","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Where, $N_B$, $N_S$, $N_T$ Total number of buyers, sellers, and trades; $B_i^Q$ kWh quantity demanded by buyer i; $S_j^Q$ kWh quantity supplied by seller j; $B_i^{Qfill}$ Cleared kWh quantity for buyer i; $\\leq B_i^Q$; $S_j^{Qfill}$ Cleared kWh quantity for seller j; $\\leq S_j^Q$; $T_m^Q$ Total kWh quantity transacted for trade m."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-20","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3","anchor_text":"the interval: NT m = 1 TmQ *TmP Pseed = NT Q m = 1 Tm (10) Because Pseed is not available for the fi","equation_id":"Eq. (10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Since discriminatory auction mechanisms do not have a uniform market clearing price at each auction interval, the historical market price is determined by the weighted average of all transactions during the interval: $P_{seed} = \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{N_T} T_m^Q * T_m^P}{\\sum_{m=1}^{N_T} T_m^Q}$ (10)"}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Discriminatory k-DA in the studied P2P solar market, using historical prices for preference-factor or game-theoretic bidding. | Initialization of the seed signal for preference-factor and game-theoretic bidding in the studied P2P solar market. | The modeled game-theoretic bidding strategies for buyers and sellers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"paper_scope_note":"The four auctions are kept separate; the time-period conditions of marginal index, buy/sell eligibility, price bound, shortfall subsidy, and historical price are retained. What is cited is the mechanism description given in the paper and is not expanded to all VCG definitions."}});
